{
  "id": "COMPOUND:17374 - PROTEIN:5187",
  "verbalization": "Mollicellin N is implicated in the pathogenesis of NCI-H2227 through multiple mechanistic routes. The evidence suggests that Mollicellin N acts as a target for Racotumomab, which in turn targets NCI-H2227, and also indirectly through palmarumycin CP18, which also targets NCI-H2227. These pathways highlight a potential role for Mollicellin N in modulating the activity of Racotumomab, which may exert its effects on NCI-H2227 via a mechanism involving the Rac1 signaling pathway. The integration of these targets indicates that Mollicellin N may influence the biological processes that drive the progression of NCI-H2227, potentially through the modulation of Racotumomab’s activity. The evidence supports a mechanistic link between Mollicellin N and NCI-H2227, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
